Yes. The personal Jenkins pipeline now has a `Parallel C regressions` stage after the ordinary C regressions.

It:

- compiles the eight manifest-selected tests;
- runs four-rank MPI baseline cases;
- checks the candidate outputs against them;
- archives `ci-parallel-regression-summary.txt` and parallel regression databases;
- uses `PERSONAL_MPIEXEC`, defaulting to the workspace OpenMPI launcher.

I also made it compatible with a baseline that predates `--parallel`: the candidate `runregression` driver runs the baseline source/install tree for that half of the comparison.

Updated [jenkinsfile.personal](/Users/mfrancis/Documents/gkeyll/code/gkeyll_v0/gkeyll/ci/jenkins/jenkinsfile.personal:116) and [README.personal.md](/Users/mfrancis/Documents/gkeyll/code/gkeyll_v0/gkeyll/ci/jenkins/README.personal.md:60). `git diff --check` passes. The stage becomes active when the personal Jenkins job loads this revision of its trusted pipeline script.

